      <section class="peg-sample__section">
        <h3 class="peg-sample__heading">
          5-Year Revenue &amp; EBITDA Estimates: Growth Sputters to 12% &mdash; Can ARPU
          Expansion Offset Stagnant Supplier Additions?
        </h3>
        <p class="peg-sample__subheading">Executive Snapshot:</p>
        <ul class="peg-sample__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Thesis:</strong> Indiamart is transitioning from a volume-led growth story
            to an ARPU-led cash compounder. With standalone collection growth decelerating to
            8% (Q2 FY26) and paying supplier growth nearly stalling (+2% YoY), the company is
            relying heavily on pricing power within its Gold/Platinum tiers (Top 10% contribute
            ~47% of revenue).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Key Driver:</strong> ARPU Expansion (~65% of future growth). With volume
            growth capped by high churn in the 'Silver' bucket, future revenue hinges on moving
            existing 222K suppliers up the value chain.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Critical Dependency:</strong> Churn Management. Management has admitted that
            churn in the monthly/annual Silver bucket remains &ldquo;stubborn.&rdquo; If this
            bleeds into Gold/Platinum tiers, the thesis breaks.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Watch:</strong> Standalone Collection Growth, currently lagging at 8-10%;
            needs to cross 15% to justify premium valuations.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="peg-sample__section">
        <h3 class="peg-sample__heading">Competitive Position &amp; Scenario Probabilities</h3>
        <p class="peg-sample__text">
          Competitive Position: Wide Moat (Network Effects) &mdash; The platform holds a dominant
          liquidity advantage with 222K paying suppliers and 42M active buyers. However, the moat
          is Stable rather than widening. While network effects protect against new entrants, they
          are not currently driving <em>new</em> usage velocity at the bottom of the pyramid
          (Silver tier churn is high), indicating saturation or value-proposition mismatch for
          smaller SMEs.
        </p>
        <div class="peg-sample__table_wrapper">
          <table class="peg-sample__table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Scenario</th>
                <th>Probability</th>
                <th>Key Drivers</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Base Case</td>
                <td>55-60%</td>
                <td>
                  Supplier base grows 3-4% CAGR; Revenue growth driven by 8-10% ARPU hikes;
                  Margins stabilize ~35% due to reduced acquisition spend.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Bear Case</td>
                <td>25-30%</td>
                <td>
                  Elevated risk. Triggered if Standalone Collections growth stays &lt;10% for 2
                  more quarters OR if entry-level churn forces price rollbacks. (See Section 5).
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Bull Case</td>
                <td>15-20%</td>
                <td>
                  Requires specific breakout in 'Busy Infotech' scaling (&gt;30% CAGR) AND
                  successful stabilization of Silver bucket churn leading to &gt;6K net
                  adds/quarter.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

