      <section class="peg-sample__section">
        <h3 class="peg-sample__heading">Key Assumptions &amp; Risk Assessment</h3>

        <p class="peg-sample__subheading">4.1 Revenue Growth Assumptions</p>
        <ul class="peg-sample__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Supplier Stagnation:</strong> Projections assume paying suppliers grow at a
            pedestrian 3-4% CAGR. Management's pivot to &ldquo;quality over quantity&rdquo;
            (reducing suppliers introduced per buyer from 9-10 to 4-5) explicitly limits volume
            explosion to preserve buyer experience.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Pricing Power:</strong> Assumes 6-8% annual ARPU increase. If macro headwinds
            force a price rollback to retain Silver customers, the Base Case is invalid.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Busy Infotech:</strong> Assumed to grow at 20%+; however, recent policy
            changes (channel partner payout restructuring in Nov '24) create short-term noise.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="peg-sample__subheading">4.2 Margin Trajectory Rationale</p>
        <ul class="peg-sample__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Cost Control Floor:</strong> Q2 FY26 EBITDA margin was ~33% (Consolidated)
            and ~32% (Standalone). Management guided that margins remain elevated due to
            <em>lower</em> subscriber acquisition costs (deliberately slowing sales spend).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Terminal Margin:</strong> Capped at 40%. The business has immense operating
            leverage, but sustaining &gt;40% usually invites aggressive competition or requires
            massive reinvestment.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="peg-sample__subheading">4.3 Key Risks to Estimates</p>
        <ul class="peg-sample__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Churn Persistence:</strong> If churn moves from the &ldquo;Silver&rdquo;
            bucket (entry-level) to the &ldquo;Gold&rdquo; bucket, the 60% revenue driver (ARPU)
            collapses.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Collections Lag:</strong> Standalone collections grew only 8% in Q2 FY26.
            Revenue lags collections. If collections don't accelerate, FY27 revenue estimates are
            at risk.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="peg-sample__subheading">4.4 Execution/Credibility Note</p>
        <ul class="peg-sample__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Adjustment Applied:</strong> Estimates are heavily discounted from implied
            management aspirations. While management targets &ldquo;double-digit&rdquo; customer
            growth historically, actual net adds (2K-3K/quarter) imply only ~4-5% growth. We have
            modeled the <em>actual</em> trajectory (3-4%), not the <em>aspiration</em>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="peg-sample__subheading">4.5 Data Limitations</p>
        <ul class="peg-sample__list">
          <li>
            <strong>Churn Granularity:</strong> Exact churn rates by specific tier (Silver Monthly
            vs Annual vs Gold) are not disclosed, forcing analyst estimates based on qualitative
            commentary.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

