 2026): The other big recent positive development, which happened in Q4 is the notification of the Ind AS standard or the IFRS 17 global standard, which is now effective April 2026.&quot;], &quot;Key Quote&quot;: [&quot;With Niva Bupa, our retail health growth for the same period was in excess of 40%, while the industry retail health growth in H2 was about 30% [1]&quot;], &quot;Sentiment&quot;: [&quot;Positive&quot;, &quot;Strong 27.4% GWP growth [2], 80% PAT growth [3], and market share gains to 10.4% [4] demonstrate execution confidence. Forward guidance of 99% combined ratio by FY&#x27;29 [5] and mid-to-high teens ROE reflects conviction. Commission regulation remains uncertain but manageable given volume-growth experience from GST [6].&quot;], &quot;Retail Health Dominance Powers Profitability Surge&quot;: [&quot;FY&#x27;26 GWP INR 9,433 crores (+27.4%) [2]; PAT INR 366 crores (+80% YoY, +90% in Q4) [3]; ROE achieved 10.7% (double-digit milestone) [7]&quot;, &quot;Retail health premium INR 6,582 crores (+35% FY&#x27;26) [8]; H2 growth exceeded 40% vs industry 30% [1]; market share expanded to 10.1% full-year and 10.4% in Q4 [4]&quot;, &quot;New-to-renewal mix 40-60 [9]; long-term policies stable at ~20% of business [10]; fresh business includes broad income segment coverage&quot;], &quot;Expense Ratio Compression &amp; Margin Expansion&quot;: [&quot;Combined ratio improved 160 bps to 101.4% under IFRS [11]; expense ratio fell 530 bps to 33.7% (from 39.2%) [12]&quot;, &quot;Three drivers: mix shift to lower-cost renewals [13], fixed overhead leverage (6-7% growth vs 27% GWP growth) [14], and 30+ AI/Gen AI pilots across value chain [15]&quot;, &quot;FY&#x27;29 targets: 99% combined ratio [5] with 200-300 bps further expense ratio improvement; loss ratio stable to +100-150 bps; translates to mid-to-high teens ROE vs 11% today&quot;], &quot;Multichannel Distribution &amp; Growth Levers&quot;: [&quot;FY&#x27;26 additions: 58,000 agents [16], 50+ brokers, 23 financial institutions; Bharat strategy focus on Tier 3+ cities showing early success [17]; digital channels demonstrating faster growth rates&quot;, &quot;Banca channel showing 46% retail new business growth [18]; diversified mix reduces concentration; management confident RBI banca guidelines won&#x27;t impact retail cross-sell&quot;, &quot;Product innovation targeting new income segments; testing new channel archetypes with pilot-to-scale approach&quot;], &quot;Hospital Empanelment &amp; Care Standardization&quot;: [&quot;2,500 hospitals empanelled (MoU signed/ready) [19] targeting 5,000 in next 4-5 months [20]; mid-segment hospital focus to enhance access outside top-20 chains&quot;, &quot;Seven infection admission protocols live (9 months) [21]; robotic surgery and modern cancer treatment protocols in advanced stage [22]; aims to optimize cost and improve transparency&quot;, &quot;Group health loss ratio 60.5% [23]; retail 66.8% [24] with post-monsoon seasonality; renewal book combined ratio stable 97%-98% [25]; preferred provider network in 49 cities with 20% claim volume [26]&quot;], &quot;Growth Catalysts: Near to Long-Term&quot;: [&quot;Near-term (&lt;1 year): Bharat geographic expansion, continued multichannel distribution additions, digital acceleration&quot;, &quot;Medium-term (1-3 years): Sustained 25% annual growth toward INR 15,000-16,000 crores GWP; product extension to new customer segments; channel innovation scaling&quot;, &quot;Long-term (&gt;3 years): Industry retail growth expected 17%-19% CAGR [27]; Niva Bupa positioned as digital-first, cost-efficient insurer with expanded hospital ecosystem&quot;], &quot;Capital Strength &amp; Financial Position&quot;: [&quot;Solvency ratio 2.49x [28] well above 1.5x regulatory minimum; AUM INR 9,670 crores [29]; investment yield 7.2% annualized [29]&quot;, &quot;IFRS 17 adoption effective April 2026 [30] brings transparency and standardization; Niva Bupa already reporting on Ind AS basis [31]&quot;], &quot;Industry 