                            <button type="button" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#concall_summary" data-content="{&quot;Sentiment&quot;: [&quot;Positive&quot;, &quot;Management expresses excitement about health insurance opportunities and confidence in their business model to deliver multi-stakeholder results, despite challenges and regulatory changes.&quot;], &quot;Financial Performance - FY25&quot;: [&quot;GWP grew by 32% on a like-to-like basis to Rs. \\\&quot;7406\\\&quot; crores. [1]&quot;, &quot;IFRS Profit After Tax (PAT) increased by 91% to Rs. \\\&quot;203\\\&quot; crores. [2]&quot;, &quot;Profit under iGAAP registered a significant growth of 161% from Rs. \\\&quot;82\\\&quot; crores to Rs. \\\&quot;214\\\&quot; crores. [3]&quot;, &quot;Net Earned Premium grew by 28% to Rs. \\\&quot;4894\\\&quot; crores. [4]&quot;, &quot;Investment yield was 7.4% with AUM of Rs. \\\&quot;8175\\\&quot; crores.&quot;, &quot;Solvency ratio stood at 3.03x against the regulatory minimum of 1.50x.&quot;], &quot;Key Performance Indicators&quot;: [&quot;Claims settlement ratio remained high at 92.4%.&quot;, &quot;Weighted average NPS improved to 55 from 50 in FY24.&quot;, &quot;Retail market share increased from 9.1% in FY24 to 9.4% in FY25. [5]&quot;, &quot;Auto adjudication rate on claims moved up to 28.5%.&quot;], &quot;Loss Ratio Analysis&quot;: [&quot;Overall IFRS loss ratio increased from 63% to 63.8%.&quot;, &quot;Retail loss ratio increased from 65% to 66%.&quot;, &quot;Group loss ratio increased from 57.7% to 58.2%.&quot;], &quot;Expense Management&quot;: [&quot;Expense of management ratio improved by 190 bps to 37.4%. [6]&quot;, &quot;Confident of achieving the allowable expense ratio in the current financial year.&quot;], &quot;Medical Inflation&quot;: [&quot;Average claim size grew by 5%, representing unit cost inflation. [7]&quot;, &quot;Provider management strategy is driven by data analytics for targeted negotiations.&quot;, &quot;Focus on quality treatment at affordable cost through Preferred Provider Network (PPN).&quot;], &quot;Growth Drivers &amp; Strategy&quot;: [&quot;Retail segment constituted 65.5% of the product mix.&quot;, &quot;Launched a new product &#x27;Rise&#x27; targeting the underserved &#x27;Missing Middle&#x27; population.&quot;, &quot;Expanding distribution network by adding agents and partners.&quot;, &quot;Health and wellness ecosystem delivered through customer app with over 11 million downloads.&quot;], &quot;Group Health Insurance&quot;: [&quot;Growth in group health was driven by employer-employee segment.&quot;, &quot;Secured two large corporate accounts valuing wellness ecosystem and total cost of ownership platform.&quot;, &quot;Contribution towards the group side has gone up by 2.5% due to two large groups picked up in the last quarter.&quot;], &quot;Multi-Year Policies&quot;: [&quot;Multi-year policy proportion is around 20%.&quot;, &quot;Change in accounting may naturally tone down the multiyear policy business as distributors now may not get the full remuneration but will get it annually.&quot;], &quot;Industry Trends &amp; Challenges&quot;: [&quot;Addressed concerns about negative press and perception issues in the health insurance industry.&quot;, &quot;Acknowledged that while the absolute count of complaints has increased because of growth, key KPIs like claim settlement rates and complaints per policy have improved.&quot;, &quot;Reiterated focus on managing fraud, waste, and abuse in the third-party payer system.&quot;, &quot;Affirmed belief that the industry is managing these issues effectively.&quot;], &quot;citations&quot;: [&quot;[1] - So we closed last year in terms of GWP at Rs.7,406 crores, a growth rate of 32% without the \u201c1/N\u201d accounting change.&quot;, &quot;[2] - We closed the year on an IFRS profit after tax of Rs.203.3 crores on a full financial year basis.&quot;, &quot;[3] - The profit under iGAAP has also registered a significant growth from a profit of Rs.82 crores in the last financial year to Rs.214 crores in the current financial year, resulting in around 161% improvement.&quot;, &quot;[4] - Net Earned Premium grew by 28% to Rs.4,894 crores.&quot;, &quot;[5] - We also grew our retail market share from 9.1% in FY24 to 9.4% on a full year basis.&quot;, &quot;[6] - So the expense of management ratio for FY25 is 37.4%; there is an improvement of 190 basis points over the last financial year where it was 39.3%.&quot;, &quot;[7] - The average claim size, which is a good proxy for medical inflation that we experienced in our portfolio, grew by 5% and broadly the CAGR on this has been about 6.5%, 7% on our portfolio.&quot;]}" data-year="2025" data-month="Mar">
