                            <button type="button" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#concall_summary" data-content="{&quot;Management Consistency Check&quot;: [&quot;**Change in Multi-Year Policy Strategy** - In the Q3 FY&#x27;25 call (Dec 2024), management stated the fundamental determinant of driving multi-year policies is the economic value they deliver. In the Q4 FY&#x27;25 (Mar 2025) call, they indicated multi-year policy proportion was around 20%, a decrease from previous levels, and the change wasn&#x27;t a conscious decision but due to distributors receiving remuneration annually rather than upfront. By Q1 FY&#x27;26 (June 2025) call, they are strategically moving down the multiyear policy.&quot;, &quot;**Unexplained Decrease in Banca Channel Growth** - During the Q3 FY&#x27;25 (Dec 2024) call, management indicated that, the bancassurance model is working well. However, In the Q1 FY&#x27;26 (June 2025) call, Ananga Rana from A91 Partners asked a question regarding the bank channel, what would the rough growth look like for banca?, to which Ankur Kharbanda responded &#x27;Our growth on the banca side is also strong. We are growing at a 20% plus on the banca side as well.&#x27; , despite this growth number seeming high, it is lower than the overall retail growth rate of 32% which suggests a slow down in the Banca channel, with no explanation.&quot;, &quot;**Halting of Auto-Adjudication and Impact of Reserve** - In Q3 FY&#x27;25 (Dec 2024), management highlighted progress in technology with 28.6% auto-adjudication rate. However, in Q1 FY&#x27;26 (June 2025), they admitted suspending the service due to information security reviews, impacting SLAs and increasing outstanding claims. Contradicting this, in the Q1 FY&#x27;26 call, Vishwanath stated that there were no abnormal trend either in incidence rate or average claim size. Additionally, in the Q1 FY&#x27;26 call, Vishwanath mentioned a 2% increase in retail loss ratio, with the biggest contributor being strengthening of reserve, further contradicting Bhabatosh who said this does not get impacted by 1/n accounting&quot;, &quot;**Inconsistent Communication on Group Business Pricing Strategy** - In the Q4 FY&#x27;25 (Mar 2025) call, management emphasized disciplined pricing in employer-employee group business. However, in the Q1 FY&#x27;26 (June 2025) call, when questioned about competition hinting at price aggression in group business, management stated their focus is on the SME segment where price sensitivity is lower, with large accounts being opportunistic, implying a shift in strategy without explicit acknowledgement.&quot;, &quot;**AUM Growth Discrepancy** - Ananga Rana asked the question in the Q4 FY&#x27;25 call (Mar 2025), AUM has grown much faster than GDP, management responded, it is because of the primary capital raise we had. If you adjust for that, it is in line with our GWP growth, however, in Q1 FY&#x27;26 (June 2025), AUM was constant and Vishwanath responded &#x27;This is because of some reinsurance payment. There is annual settlement. We made some sizable reinsurance payment. That&#x27;s why on quarter-on-quarter, you will see that it is stable.&#x27;&quot;], &quot;summary&quot;: &quot;{\n  \&quot;Sentiment\&quot;: [\n    \&quot;Positive\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Justification: Management highlights strong growth (28% overall, 32% in retail health), significant increase in IFRS PAT (from INR36 crores to INR70 crores), and improvement in the combined ratio. They express confidence in bringing down the expense of management ratio within regulatory limits and are optimistic about future trends and initiatives.\&quot;\n  ],\n  \&quot;Financial Performance - Q1 FY&#x27;26\&quot;: [\n    \&quot;GWP grew by \\\&quot;28%\\\&quot; (like-to-like basis) [1].\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Retail health business grew by \\\&quot;32%\\\&quot; (like-to-like basis) [2].\&quot;,\n    \&quot;IFRS PAT increased to INR \\\&quot;70\\\&quot; crores from INR \\\&quot;36\\\&quot; crores in Q1 FY&#x27;25.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Combined ratio (IFRS) improved to \\\&quot;103.2%\\\&quot; from \\\&quot;103.9%\\\&quot;.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Retail market share increased from \\\&quot;9.9%\\\&quot; to \\\&quot;10%\\\&quot;.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Investment yield on annualized basis in Q1 is \\\&quot;7.3%\\\&quot; with AUM of more than INR \\\&quot;8,100\\\&quot; crores.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Solvency ratio is at \\\&quot;2.86x\\\&quot;.\&quot;\n  ],\n  \&quot;Accounting and IFRS Impact\&quot;: [\n    \&quot;Multiyear accounting changes continue to create noise in reported numbers.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;IFRS is considered a better reflection of financials; the company continues to report on an IFRS basis.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;The Insurance Contract IFRS 17 adjustment is about INR \\\&quot;179\\\&quot; crores due to UPR on 1/n basis.\&quot;\n  ],\n  \&quot;Product and Pricing Strategy\&quot;: [\n    \&quot;Product mix: \\\&quot;67%\\\&quot; retail, \\\&quot;31%\\\&quot; group, and \\\&quot;2%\\\&quot; travel and PA.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Executed a \\\&quot;7%\\\&quot; price increase on ReAssure 2.0 in Q1 [3].\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Average ticket size per policy is consistent on a like-to-like basis (excluding 1/n impact).\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Following LTV approach for pricing; zonal-wise pricing is an extension of LTV.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;The price hike, the core objective is to negate inflation, the underlying medical inflation.\&quot;\n  ],\n  \&quot;Customer Engagement and Health Ecosystem\&quot;: [\n    \&quot;\\\&quot;12.3\\\&quot; million health app downloads and \\\&quot;5.7\\\&quot; lakh monthly active users.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Over \\\&quot;50,000\\\&quot; health checkups and \\\&quot;6,000\\\&quot; doctor consults per month through the app.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Launched a chronic condition management program in Q1.\&quot;,\n    \&quot;Blended NPS score stands at \\\&quot;57\\\&quot; at the end of Q1; cashless claims discharge NPS in the high 60s.\&quot;\n  ],\n  \&quo