rowth overall as a company for quarter 1 was 28%.&quot;, &quot;[2] - And within that, our retail health growth -- our retail health business grew at 32%.&quot;, &quot;[3] - In Q1, specifically on one of our flagship products, which is ReAssure 2.0, we did execute a 7% increase in Q1.&quot;, &quot;[4] - Our growth on the banca side is also strong. We are growing at a 20% plus on the banca side as well.&quot;, &quot;[5] - On account of a bunch of information security assurance reviews specifically with third parties, we did suspend the auto-adjudication service&quot;, &quot;[6] - Retail IFRS ratio is around 68% and group would be around 61% broadly.&quot;, &quot;[7] - Last year, it was more like -- retail was around 66% and group was around 58%.&quot;]}" data-year="2025" data-month="Jun">
