%&quot;, &quot;IFRS PAT more than doubled from \u20b960 crores (H1 FY&#x27;25) to \u20b9132 crores (H1 FY&#x27;26) [14], demonstrating significant margin expansion&quot;, &quot;Combined Insurance Service Ratio improved 105 basis points to 103.1% (from 104.2%) [15], driven by 2.3% reduction in expense ratio offsetting 1.2% increase in loss ratio [16]&quot;, &quot;Expense of Management Ratio improved 3.7% to 36.3% (from 40%) [17], with expenses growing low single digit while GWP grew 23%, showing strong operating leverage&quot;, &quot;Retail loss ratio stable at 68.1% versus 68% in H1 FY&#x27;25 [18]; overall loss ratio increase driven entirely by group business mix shift [19]&quot;, &quot;Allowable EOM ratio at 35.8%; currently 50 basis points above regulatory limit but management confident of bringing within glide path by FY&#x27;26 end [20]&quot;, &quot;Solvency ratio healthy at 2.85x as of September 30, 2025 [21]&quot;], &quot;Retail Health Insurance Segment Delivering Volume and Value Growth&quot;: [&quot;28% retail GWP growth comprised of 6% to 7% value growth and approximately 20% volume (lives) growth [22], with balance from ticket size improvement&quot;, &quot;Average ticket size per retail policy exceeds \u20b931,000, industry-leading metric [23]; 83% of policies have sum insured of \u20b91 million or above [24]&quot;, &quot;ReAssure 3.0 next-generation product launched in Q2 with strong market reception [25]; supported by new microservices-based core system enabling faster product development [26]&quot;, &quot;Settlement ratio for claims at 95.2% in Q2 [27]; weighted average NPS across 35 customer touchpoints improved to 57 for H1 [28]&quot;, &quot;Direct digital business growing at 1.5x organizational average growth rate [29]; direct business appears lower due to 1/N accounting impact rather than strategic shift&quot;, &quot;Porting policies stable at 20% to 25% range [30], with percentage potentially declining; indicates stable customer base without exces