nsurance service ratio for H1 improved by more than 100 basis points to 103.1%&quot;, &quot;[16] - increase in overall loss ratio by 1.2%, offset by reduction in expense ratio by 2.3%&quot;, &quot;[17] - year-on-year improvement in expense ratio to tune of 3.7% with H1 EOM being 36.3% versus 40%&quot;, &quot;[18] - retail loss ratio for first half current financial year is 68.1%, in line with last financial year H1 of 68%&quot;, &quot;[19] - 1.2% increase largely coming from group because of mix change, where group has gone up&quot;, &quot;[20] - allowable EOM ratio comes to 35.8%, above allowed by 50 basis points, confident of bringing within limit&quot;, &quot;[21] - Solvency ratio is at healthy level of 2.85x as on 30th September 2025&quot;, &quot;[22] - 28% retail growth comprised 6% to 7% value growth and balance from volume and ticket size improvement&quot;, &quot;[23] - industry-leading ATS at more than INR31,000&quot;, &quot;[24] - close to 83% of our policies have sum insured 1 million or above&quot;, &quot;[25] - launched next-generation retail health insurance product, ReAssure 3.0 with very good reception&quot;, &quot;[26] - gone live with modern microservices-based core system, transformational for product launches&quot;, &quot;[27] - settlement rate for Q2 on claims was 95.2%&quot;, &quot;[28] - weighted average NPS improved to 57 for H1 across 35 critical customer touch points&quot;, &quot;[29] - growth of business from direct digital for first half almost 1.5x of average growth&quot;, &quot;[30] - porting percentage has been stable, between 20% and 25% where our porting has been&quot;, &quot;[31] - in H1 more than 13 million downloads of health ecosystem customer app&quot;, &quot;[32] - more than 51,000 health check-ups every month and 6,700 doctor consults monthly&quot;, &quot;[33] - added one more city in preferred provider network, now in 44 cities&quot;, &quot;[34] - about 17% of our claims in cities where PPN is present go through these PPN hospitals&quot;, &quot;[35] - difference of about 10% to 15% PPN versus quaternary tertiary care facility in claim costs&quot;, &quot;[36] - set up an AI lab to explore many exciting capabilities that Gen AI has to offer&quot;, &quot;[37] - implementing favourable claims experience discount and experience basis when repricing products&quot;, &quot;[38] - if somebody does 10,000 steps daily on customer app, eligible for high as 30% discount at renewal&quot;, &quot;[39] - group business growth 13% for H1 and 6% Y-o-Y in Q2 without 1/N&quot;, &quot;[40] - wherever combined ratio is within acceptable side, we do that, not just looking at LR&quot;, &quot;[41] - more than 2/3 of our business by policy count comes from SME, 70% to 75% or higher&quot;, &quot;[42] - SME growth has been close to 50%, offsetting slower overall group growth&quot;, &quot;[43] - SME sourced through direct-to-consumer, bank partners, agency network, and broker network&quot;, &quot;[44] - group loss ratio increased to 60.9% from 56%, H1 FY&#x27;26 versus H1 FY&#x27;25&quot;, &quot;[45] - roughly one-third two-third split between employer-employee and affinity business&quot;, &quot;[46] - Annualized investment yield for H1 is 7.3% with AUM of INR8,482 crores&quot;, &quot;[47] - Duration would be 4.5 years with maturity 61 months for debt portfolio&quot;, &quot;[48] - reinsurance treaty settlement was on annual basis, now quarterly from May 2025&quot;, &quot;[49] - incidence rates and average claim size range bound and within stable trend&quot;, &quot;[50] - loss ratio trend perspective improving in recent months downward trend&quot;, &quot;[51] - outstanding claims provision on higher side, largely released as auto adjudication stabilized&quot;, &quot;[52] - standardization protocols for 7 conditions and 10, 12 diagnosis codes adopted by SAHI&quot;, &quot;[53] - close to 3,500 or 4,000 hospitals applied under common empanelment initiative&quot;, &quot;[54] - stick to long-term guidance FY &#x27;29 mid t